# JetNote Kotlin / Compose

## File placement

- Screen composables and `*ViewModel.kt` live in `com.hmyh.jetnote.screen`.
- Shared inputs/buttons: `components/` (`NoteInputText`, `NoteButton`).
- Do not put business models in `screen/` — use `model/` or `data/`.

## Compose

- Wrap app UI in `JetNoteTheme`; use Material 3 (`MaterialTheme`, `TopAppBar`, `LazyColumn`).
- Pass events up: `onAddNote: (Note) -> Unit`, `onRemoveNote: (Note) -> Unit` (see `NoteScreen`).
- Use `@Preview` with `NoteDataSource().loadNotes()` for screen previews.

## ViewModel

- Extend `ViewModel`; hold list state with `mutableStateListOf` until Room/Flow migration.
- Inject dependencies via Hilt when wiring `AppModule` — prefer `@HiltViewModel` + constructor inject over `NoteDataSource()` in `init`.

## Models

```kotlin
// model/ — non-null fields for active Note instances
data class Note(val title: String, val description: String, ...)

// data/ — nullable optional fields
data class UserData(val name: String? = null, val age: Int? = null, val nrc: String? = null)
```
